  "verbalization": "Cefprozil, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is linked to Staphylococcal Infection through a chain of indications that involve bacterial infections. The evidence suggests that Cefprozil may be repurposed to treat infections caused by Staphylococcus species, as it is indicated for Streptococcal Infection in two separate paths. In both cases, the antibiotic is associated with a downstream infection, indicating a potential mechanism of action or therapeutic effect. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to Staphylococcal Infection suggests that Cefprozil may have broad antimicrobial activity against staphylococcal pathogens, possibly through inhibition of bacterial cell wall synthesis or other mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the antibiotic's potential to treat a range of bacterial infections, including those caused by Staphylococcus, by leveraging its existing indications in other infections.",
